Export Date: 25 September 2026
Cited By: 3
Funding details: RWTH Aachen University; Institut de Radioprotection et de SÛreté Nucléaire, IRSN; Keck Carbon Cycle AMS Laboratory in Irvine, California, USA
Funding text 1: This study is co-funded by the RWTH Aachen University (Germany) and the IRSN (France). We thank the Keck Carbon Cycle AMS Laboratory in Irvine, California, USA, for the radiocarbon analysis. Our sincere thanks go to all individuals who actively participated and contributed to the trenching and geophysical field campaigns, including the landowner of the trenching site, Martin Cammerer, as well as land users Sebastian and Josef Sch\u00E4chtele, the Thomas family for their assistance with excavation, and Joachim Eisel, the municipal administrator of Tunsel. We thank Nina Engels and Lisa Feist for their assistance in the trenching campaign. Furthermore, we appreciate the insightful discussions held in the field with Frank Lehmkuhl, Gordon Seitz, J\u00E9rome van der Woerd, and Anne-Sophie M\u00E9riaux. Finally, we are grateful to Manuel Diercks and an anonymous reviewer for their detailed and constructive feedback, which has significantly improved this manuscript.
