@inproceedings{Yamazaki2025,
   abstract = {An Mw 7.1 earthquake hit the southern Tibetan Plateau of China on January 7, 2025. The earthquake was caused by a normal fault system with a shallow depth. Soon after the earthquake, ALOS-2 satellite observed the affected area with the Strip-Map fine mode. This study conducted a DInSAR analysis using the pre- and post-event PALSAR-2 SLC data. A clear displacement pattern of normal faulting was obtained from the analysis. The estimated LOS displacement agreed well with the location of the reported surface faulting. The fault plane was estimated by a linear inversion of the DInSAR results using an elastic dislocation model. The changes of the ground surface due to geological hazards and building damages were also estimated from the reduction of coherence and they were compared with optical satellite images. © 2025 IEICE Electronics Society.},
