Funding text 2: The work presented in this paper represents several years of effort. The philosophy and methodology with which we approached the study of the surface rupture of the historical 1946 Chatkal earthquake were greatly inspired by the experience M.R. gained while working with P. Tapponnier along the rupture of the 1934 Bihar-Nepal and the 1931 Fuyun earthquakes, two large historical earthquakes. We extend our sincere gratitude to the Institute of Seismology at the National Academy of Sciences of Kyrgyzstan (Bishkek) for their long-term partnership and support throughout our field campaign with on-the-ground assistance that was essential to the success of this work. This work was granted by the Centre National d\u2019 Etudes Spatiales CNES (HIDATHSA project). This work benefited also from the French CNES-DINAMIS program ISIS to acquire the Pleiades images. DINAMIS is funded by CNES, CNRS, IGN, IRD, INRAE, CIRAD. This project has received funding from \u201CExcellence Initiative\u201D of Aix Marseille University A*MIDEX, a french \u201CInvestissement d'avenir\u201D program and by the National Program TelluS-ALEAS of CNRS/INSU. We thank the LMC14 staff (Laboratoire de Mesure du Carbone-14), ARTEMIS national facility, (LSCE-(CNRS-CEA-UVSQ)-IRD-IRSN-MC) for the results obtained with the accelerator mass spectrometry method. We would like to thank C. Gr\u00FCtzner, E. Nissen, an anonymous reviewer, and the editors for their constructive comments and discussions during the preparation and revision of the manuscript.
Correspondence Address: M. Rizza; Département des sciences de la Terre et de l'atmosphère, UQAM, Montréal, France; email: rizza.magali@uqam.ca},
