Funding text 1: We are most grateful to the executive management of the Turkish Petroleum Corp. for granting us the permission to use the 3-D PSTM seismic image volume, provide the computer resources and staff time to conduct this project, and grant the permission to publish this work. We thank O. Tan for providing the up-to-date earthquake catalogue for the Anatolian Plate and the Marmara Region ( Tan, 2021), and Y. Zhao for generating the hypocenter maps shown in Fig. 15. We also acknowledge the use of Digital Elevation Model (DEM) from Shuttle Radar Topography Mission (SRTM) acquired by the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration (NASA) The information on this data set can be found in the link https://topex.ucsd.edu/WWW_html/srtm30_plus.html. All data are derived from public domain sources and these data are also in the public domain; Created By: Joseph J. Becker and David T. Sandwell; Creation Date: 2011-12-16. We are grateful to H. Karabulut, S. \u00D6zalaybey, A. Kocao\u011Flu, A. Taranc\u0131o\u011Flu, S. Ergintav, O. Tan, and R. Armijo for extensive discussions regarding the tectonics of Marmara Basin. We are also grateful to T. Dooley, P. Mann, and C. Scholz for their insight in aspects of fault mechanism at large and strike-slip tectonism, specifically. We extend our special thanks to Geoteric for providing us with a research license for the 3-D AI fault interpretation software module. Finally, we are indeed grateful to reviewers Fabien Caroir and Laurent Jolivet, and Editor Gregory Houseman, for helpful and constructive comments which significantly improved the manuscript. We declare that there is no real or perceived financial conflict of interest for any author.
