@inproceedings{Tian2025,
   abstract = {Taking the infrared remote sensing brightness temperature data of geostationary meteorological satellite FY-2C/E as the data source, this paper proposed a new processing and analysis method, that is, wavelet difference analysis combined with relative power spectrum method, and obtained the vertical section analysis chart and the temporal-spatial evolution of brightness temperature in Yushu M7.1 earthquake. The results showed that the anomaly belt of brightness temperature and its variation process related to seismic activity could be clearly identified from the brightness temperature difference analysis chart of vertical section of fault zone, and there existed a nearly uniform thermal belt with the fault strike in the temporal-spatial evolution map of thermal infrared anomaly. The attempt of this method in our study could provide some useful information for acquiring fault activity from infrared remote sensing data, and connect precursory anomaly, fault variation and seismic activity as a whole.  © 2025 SPIE. Downloading of the abstract is permitted for personal use only.},
